					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-29 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br>so last night the treacherous three, that is, Geo, RA and myself rocked
the Independent on Divisadero.&nbsp; big up to Mr. Lif and The Coup for
putting us on.&nbsp; much love to the bay area fam that hosted us (leonard
shek) and gave us tips on where to eat.&nbsp; <br />
<br />
golden flower in chinatown for pho.<br />
mama&#39;s in the north beach for filthy omelettes.<br />
<br />
and who could forget, the best tapsilog in the south bay not cooked by your auntie!<br />
<br />
<img src="http://www.lchances.com/images/streetlc.jpg" alt="luckychances" title="luckychances" width="250" height="171" align="middle" /><br />
<br />
that&#39;s what it do. we&#39;re about to hit up san luis obispo today to start the tour with Dan The Automator.&nbsp; we&#39;ll keep ya posted.<br />
<br />
saba<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-28 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br>hearing accounts of snow drifts in the town makes me just a little bit home sick, at least until i step outside to dimaggio park where a large group of seniors are basking in the morning sun, their tai chi postures casting long shadows across the lawn.&nbsp; <strong>north beach </strong>is certified DOAP.&nbsp; last night&#39;s dinner was the first to top salvatore&#39;s in years, and breakfast at <strong>mama&#39;s </strong>was the kind travel writers live for.&nbsp; italian folks make the greatest hosts, and it&#39;s becoming abundantly evident to me how sinatra could have left his heart in this community.<br /><br />big up&#39;s to the hawks for pulling off a miracle of sorts as the elements made it seem like they were visitors at lambeau.&nbsp; the victory was much needed to lift geo&#39;s spirits, dampened by a relentless head-cold.&nbsp; keep sendin&#39; those positive, healing-type vibes, fam.<br /><br />i&#39;m lookin&#39; forward to the reunion with <strong>boots </strong>tonight.&nbsp; rumor has it the spot is &quot;uber fresh,&quot; and speaking from recent experience, aint too much poppin&#39; in downtown frisco on a weeknight.&nbsp; bring &#39;em out, bring &#39;em out...<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-27 | Monday</font></strong><br><br>whaddup, fam.&nbsp; all&#39;s well.&nbsp; we crossed the bay bridge at the stroke of
midnight doin&#39; 80mph with sabz behind the wheel.&nbsp; an able pilot he is,
but it&#39;s geo that deserves capitano props for navigating through a
snow-storm and one hellacious construction-related traffic jam in the
oregonian mountains.&nbsp; carsickness is kryptonite.<br /><br />respect due to
the homie big L for housin&#39; us - i slept well, got a shower and i&#39;m
bouts to get mocha&#39;d up in a minute.&nbsp; after that i&#39;m trynna find some
new music to cruise to (&quot;i thought you were gonna make the tour
mixtape.&quot;&nbsp; no i thought YOU were gonna make the tour mixtape...&quot;), then
take in the sights and sounds of the bay; seein&#39; sunshine on the
rooftops and hearin&#39; kids kick it at recess has made for a beautiful
first impression.<br /><br />more later.&nbsp; i need a cup of frisco&#39;s finest.<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-24 | Friday</font></strong><br><br>award tour.<br /><br />the whole MassLine fam heads down to PDX today to rock the doug fir for all our northern oregonian brethrenian.&nbsp; after that we&#39;ll take a tour of the alternative lifestyles of eugene and share with the locals some of the sounds of seattle.<br /><br />in the bay, Blue Scholars open for Mr. Lif (big up for checkin out the showbox on wednesday, Liffy!) and The Coup <br />at The Independent and then Common Market heads south to hop on Dan The Automator&#39;s tour.<br /><br />check in with us for the next couple weeks as we will be (attempting to) update you on a daily basis about the westkoast adventures.&nbsp; maybe we&#39;ll even get some pictures.<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-22 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br>Doors are at 8pm. See you there.<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=265">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[36]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=180">[37]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=185">[38]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=190">[39]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=195">[40]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=200">[41]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=205">[42]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=210">[43]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=215">[44]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=220">[45]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=225">[46]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=230">[47]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=235">[48]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=240">[49]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=245">[50]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=250">[51]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=255">[52]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=260">[53]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=265">[54]</A> [55] <A HREF="archive.php?from=275">[56]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=280">[57]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=285">[58]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=290">[59]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=275">[&gt;&gt;]</A>  </span></p>
